  "context": {
    "model_figure": {
      "caption_latex": "Q-LACE pipeline. Report-derived weak supervision adapts a medical VLM for held-out finding-conditioned interval-change classification using 2,048 weak-training examples per run. Adaptation includes language/vision LoRA and trainable input embeddings and output head; other base weights remain frozen. Historical validation-monitoring schedules are specified in Appendix~\\ref{sec:historical_provenance}. ``No evidence'' is an appendix diagnostic, while the three change labels define the benchmark task. The illustrative radiographs are separate NIH Clinical Center images from different patients, arranged to depict input roles; they are not a real longitudinal pair or study evaluation case. NIH credit and download: \\url{https://nihcc.app.box.com/v/ChestXray-NIHCC}; \\cite{wang2017chestxray}. Author-created schematic, exported with Inkscape 1.4.4/cairo 1.18.4.",
      "caption_text": "Q-LACE pipeline. Report-derived weak supervision adapts a medical VLM for held-out finding-conditioned interval-change classification using 2,048 weak-training examples per run. Adaptation includes language/vision LoRA and trainable input embeddings and output head; other base weights remain frozen. Historical validation-monitoring schedules are specified in Appendix A.10. \"No evidence\" is an appendix diagnostic, while the three change labels define the benchmark task. The illustrative radiographs are separate NIH Clinical Center images from different patients, arranged to depict input roles; they are not a real longitudinal pair or study evaluation case. NIH credit and download: https://nihcc.app.box.com/v/ChestXray-NIHCC; [wang2017chestxray]. Author-created schematic, exported with Inkscape 1.4.4/cairo 1.18.4.",
